  "working_tree": "Uncommitted code-intelligence work; this receipt and documentation follow frozen checks.",
  "shared_implementation": "Host::execute_in owns one native transaction interpreter above ExecutionFolder and JournalBackend adapters. Local uses its original proven companion session and paired journal; Remote uses the native project folder and backend journal. The frontend submits one complete Execute for native plan version 2.",
  "contract": [
    "Paired Inspect/Load preflight checks the exact original bootstrap and private native worker preimage without admitting a worker. Inspect is compact; only full Load has a 192 MiB response limit. Expired, stale-scope, wrong-account, wrong-secret and released-worker reads reject.",
    "Both modes acquire the physical folder gate before the snapshot slot and full journal load. The common runner reloads current scope and evidence, verifies initial native review, claims current authority, executes the shared interpreter and durably releases the worker while retaining its fence.",
    "The paired root adapter retains the exact original proven session, root descriptor, native worker identity and resource-plan binding. It preserves that session while retiring overlapping peers. It does not acquire a second per-primitive lease.",
    "Native workers own accepted execution after observer loss. Both-mode real SQLite/private-HTTP/folder contracts hold a competing lease until completed mutation and durable release, reject stale queued recovery before any full load, and preserve editor/file state on rejection.",
    "A real original Local LSP/HMAC session rejects a bad manual grant without worker or file mutation, then accepts the unchanged retained review and commits its native rename and editor patch without additional LSP calls. A new worker acknowledges its accepted committed result after service shutdown and grant expiry without replaying a command.",
    "The browser companion marks an ambiguous complete Execute acknowledgement as unusable for read/replay, including a late reply. Close remains available. Current native plan-2 workflows use one Execute; explicit legacy browser recovery remains compatible.",
    "Fresh installed resource/command and declared-input workflows pass in Local and Remote modes. The Local trace requires original proof before analysis, one Execute after original-service validation on that same session, bind and close, with no browser Admit/Advance/mutable-file loop. Fault injection pauses the actual native journal primitives in both modes."
  ],
